from pathlib import Path
P=Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent/'stage/2f59a0d07a85/astraupskill'
extra={
'README.md':'''Start by drawing two topics, each with a post. Predict what happens when a client submits the second post's id while replying in the first topic. Then compare the before snapshot with the service and execute the focused lab. The expanded five-case suite also walks a valid child and a top-level reply through creation and counter updates. Finish by explaining why validating an id's existence differs from validating its relationship to another resource. This distinction transfers to comments on articles, tasks in projects and order items in carts.''',
'01-CODEBASE-MAP.md':'''The caller [createReplyAction](../src/app/actions.ts) obtains the authenticated user, reads form values, normalizes an empty parent id to undefined and calls this service. Only after success does it look up the topic slug, revalidate the page and redirect to the new post anchor. The [Prisma model](../prisma/schema.prisma) has separate topic and self-referential parent foreign keys. Neither relation compares the parent's topicId with the child's. Inside the service, notifications and trust recalculation follow the transaction; audit is last. A later failure is therefore not evidence that the already-completed transaction was rolled back.''',
'02-CONCEPTS.md':'''Consider three layers of validation. The input schema checks the shape and length of strings. The parent lookup establishes existence and topic membership. Posting rules check whether this user may contribute in the category. These checks answer different questions and should not replace each other. The new lookup occurs before the transaction, so it is not an atomic guarantee against a concurrent deletion or reassignment. The correction also does not introduce a policy for deleted, hidden or staff-only parents. Those fields exist on Post, but changing their semantics requires a separately defined visibility rule and corresponding tests.''',
'03-WORKED-CHANGE.md':'''Read the exact [original](snapshots/forum-core.ts.original.txt) beside the current function. The new query selects only topicId because that is the field needed for membership validation. It does not fetch or expose the foreign parent's content. Existing transaction writes still compute position from the final post and increment both counters. The positive test starts at position three and verifies the new payload uses position four, the same author and topic, and the requested optional parent. It also checks that the returned object is the created object, catching an accidental return-value regression that rejection-only tests would miss.''',
'04-TESTING-AND-DEBUGGING.md':'''The expanded suite has five named cases. In addition to the original refusals, it covers valid nested/top-level replies, a closed topic and a parent-query error. The success fixture supplies empty subscriptions and trust levels so actual internal orchestration can finish without native database access. It checks payload fields and both counter increments. A same-topic reply looks up its parent again during notification preparation; a top-level reply performs neither parent lookup. If this count changes, inspect the notification helper before blaming the new guard. Schemas, permissions, enum exports and external helpers remain explicit adapters; input validation and actual authorization are not proven.''',
'05-PRACTICE.md':'''Use a ten-point rubric: two points for predicting each parent branch correctly, two for locating the guard after posting rules, two for preserving creation fields and counter increments, two for explaining post-transaction effects, and two for identifying the concurrency limit. For a debugging exercise, deliberately compare the parent topic to user.id instead of topic.id, then run the lab and explain which valid case catches the mistake. Restore the code afterward. For a design exercise, propose how hidden parents should behave, identifying which permission rule and UI expectation must be clarified before implementation.''',
'06-SOLUTIONS-AND-REVIEW.md':'''For the position-three fixture, the child is created at position four. Both topic.replyCount and user.postsCreatedCount increment once. The same-topic parent is read once for the guard and once for notification preparation. With no parent id, there are no parent lookups. A closed topic stops before posting rules and parent validation; a query failure propagates unchanged before the transaction opens. The membership guard does not ensure parent visibility, nor does it lock a parent row. A senior-level review should distinguish these remaining policy and concurrency questions from the bounded invariant actually repaired.''',
'07-TRACE-LAB.md':'''The expanded lab now includes the successful transaction trace. Fill in a worksheet before running it:

| Input | Guard result | Transaction | Parent reads |
|---|---|---|---|
| No parent | Skipped | Create and counters | Zero |
| Same topic | Accepted | Create and counters | Two including notification preparation |
| Foreign topic | Error | Never entered | One |
| Missing parent | Error | Never entered | One |
| Closed topic | Earlier error | Never entered | Zero |

Separate the query-error trace from an absent row: the former preserves an operational error while the latter raises a deliberate domain error. List which layers would translate those errors for a browser. The focused test does not execute that translation.''',
'VERIFICATION.md':'''The accepted root suite uses label crud-b04-astra-runtime and executes five cases with Node's built-in test runner and experimental VM modules. Its command is `node --experimental-vm-modules --test tests/reply-parent-boundary.test.mjs` from the project root. It loads the production forum module directly through the local TypeScript loader. Internal notification/trust paths run with data adapters in positive cases; no notification is actually sent and audit persistence is substituted. Local Next.js guides were unavailable after dependency cleanup, and no Next.js route or API behavior was changed. Database foreign-key enforcement, rollback, concurrent parent changes and browser form behavior remain unexecuted.'''
}
